id: searx-lkzp
title: Ship complete SearXNG instance resources and uniform agent contracts
description: "Expose every stable read-only SearXNG application resource through typed TOON-default commands, make global machine-output flags truthful across command families, refresh the latest PM and changelog toolchain, and ship exact live/package/review/release proof without regressing search, setup, global state, or unlimited cache behavior."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[8]: agent,cli,instance-resources,pm-governance,release,searxng,toolchain,toon
created_at: "2026-07-25T22:30:26.978Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T23:13:10.266Z"
deadline: "2026-07-26T22:30:26.978Z"
assignee: codex-searxng-agent
author: codex-searxng-agent
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "Typed commands expose /healthz, /config, /engine_descriptions.json, /stats, /stats/errors, /opensearch.xml, /manifest.json, and /robots.txt with stable provenance envelopes; TOON is default and JSON or raw overrides are validated and pipe-safe; every command and subcommand has accurate detailed help and advertised global flags behave consistently; search retains all typed and raw upstream parameters plus HTML fallback; ~/.searxng-cli global settings/setup/cache contracts and zero-limit persistence remain proven; latest pm-cli and pm-changelog are installed and healthy; 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, lint, duplication, security, PM, live installed CLI, package, release, CI, review, merged-head, and release checks pass"
definition_of_ready: "All 55 PM items across all statuses and their rich fields, canonical histories and graph analytics; official current SearXNG docs/source; live instance routes; TOON specification/package; npm dependency state; repository source/tests/docs; and GitHub state were inspected with zero duplicate candidates."
goal: Complete agent-native SearXNG service parity
objective: Typed read-only resources and truthful machine contracts
value: "Agents can discover, diagnose, and consume the whole configured SearXNG service without ad hoc curl parsing"
impact: Eliminates hidden route and formatting gaps while preserving the proven search and persistence core
outcome: "A reviewed, release-ready CLI whose documented commands match actual behavior against the governed LAN instance"
why_now: "The prior release completed search and operational parity, but today's route inventory exposed stable resources with no first-class CLI command and global flags that are documented more broadly than implemented."
reviewer: github-bots
risk: high
confidence: 92
sprint: 2026-07-current-parity
release: 2026.7.26
